        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/h/w/narberth-pembrokeshire-wp/rebecca-s-cell-at-narberth-geo.jpg",
          "filename": "\"Rebecca's cell\" at Narberth - geograph.org.uk - 530506.jpg",
          "caption": "\"Rebecca's cell\"  at  Narberth In the 1830s and 40s local people in West Wales took the law into their own hands in protest against English-imposed tolls, taxes and repressive legislation. They disguised themselves in women's clothes and operated under the name of Rebecca. I do not know if there is evidence that any of the 'Rebeccas' occupied this lock-up under the town hall but the freedom fighters were active in Narberth, attacking the workhouse and the tollgate, so it is very possible that they did.",
          "alt": "\"Rebecca's cell\"  at  Narberth In the 1830s and 40s local people in West Wales took the law into their own hands in protest against English-imposed tolls, taxes and repressive legislation. They disguised themselves in women's clothes and operated under the name of Rebecca. I do not know if there is evidence that any of the 'Rebeccas' occupied this lock-up under the town hall but the freedom fighters were active in Narberth, attacking the workhouse and the tollgate, so it is very possible that they did.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 434,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "ceridwen",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%22Rebecca%27s_cell%22_at_Narberth_-_geograph.org.uk_-_530506.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
